(vector (map (:db/id -1) (:adr/id 2799007133) (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7133 — Building Structure Cleaners Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage") (:adr/status "accepted") (:adr/doc_type "adr") (:adr/date "2026-07-18") (:adr/source-format "edn") (:adr/scope (vector "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7133" "kotoba-lang/occupation")) (:adr/references (vector 2607121000 2607152500)) (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2607152500-cloud-itonami-wave4-rollout-start-amendment" "adr-2799007121-cloud-itonami-isco-7121-roofers-coverage")) (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)) (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)) (:registry/maturity :implemented) (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7133") (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7133") (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7133) (:actor/name "Building Structure Cleaning Crew Scheduling & Logistics Coordination Service") (:actor/isco-08 "7133") (:actor/wave 3) (:actor/domain :construction/building-cleaning-coordination) (:actor/robotics? true) (:actor/coordination? true) (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)) (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-site :no-actuation :unknown-op :site-mismatch :unknown-worker :worker-wrong-site :scope-exclusion-violation)) (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)) (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-cleaning-execution :execute-cleaning-work-directly :perform-building-cleaning-directly :finalize-height-work-go-no-go-decision :override-site-safety-officer-judgment :bypass-site-safety-officer-signoff :bypass-chemical-exposure-safety-review)) (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the height-work cleaning task" "proceed with the building cleaning work" "finalize the cleaning-execution decision" "finalize the height-work go/no-go decision" "finalize the height-work-execution decision" "execute the cleaning work directly" "execute the height-work directly" "perform the building cleaning directly" "dispatch the crew to perform cleaning work" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override the site-safety officer's judgment" "override the site-safety officer" "override the safety officer's height-work judgment" "bypass the site-safety officer" "bypass height-work sign-off" "bypass the chemical-exposure safety review" "bypass the chemical-handling safety judgment")) (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 10000}") (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)) (:operation/entry-point :intake) (:test/simulator :bldgclean.actor-test) (:test/counts "{:total 25, :assertions 63, :failures 0, :errors 0}") (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :worker-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation :always-escalate-safety-concern :chemical-exposure-safety-concern)) (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007133: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7133 Building Structure Cleaners job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7133\n-- Building Structure Cleaners** only. The occupation-actor track is\ncurrently working Wave3 (production/trades); ISCO Wave0/Wave1/Wave2\nare all 100% complete, and Wave3 batches 1-4 (construction/metal\ntrades 7111-7222, agriculture 6113/6129/6223/6224/6310/6320) were\nalready landed before this ADR.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7133\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7133\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Building Structure Cleaners\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]`, `:optional-technologies []` and\n`:operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit]`, and\nno `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7133` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7133` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a compound height-work and chemical-cleaning\nsafety dimension: Building Structure Cleaners wash windows and clean\nbuilding exteriors/facades at height on active job sites (one of the\nhighest fall-risk trades), and routinely apply chemical cleaning\nagents, adding a chemical-exposure risk alongside the fall-from-height\nrisk.** A wrongful automated decision here could directly endanger a\nworker's life or health. The closed op allowlist therefore must NEVER\ninclude any op that directly finalizes a cleaning-execution decision\n(including a height-work go/no-go call) or overrides a site-safety\nofficer's judgment -- such a decision must always be a hard, permanent\nblock or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This is\nthe same underlying principle the Wave4-amendment ADR\n(ADR-2607152500) established for decisions directly touching safety,\ndignity or subsistence in the human-services track, and the same\nshape ADR-2799007121 (Roofers) applied to the fall-protection safety\ndimension: this actor applies that shape to BOTH the height-work\ngo/no-go dimension AND the chemical-exposure dimension, because a\nworker's physical safety and health carries the same weight as the\ndecision classes those precedents protect.\n\n**This actor coordinates JOB-SITE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it\nnever performs building-cleaning work itself.** It is not an\nauthority to decide when or how cleaning work happens on a building\nexterior; it is a coordination layer for work-record logging, crew\nscheduling, safety-concern surfacing and cleaning-materials/\nequipment-order coordination, all gated behind an independent\ngovernor.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7121)\n(Roofers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph, full doc set: README, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,\nGOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later), SECURITY.md,\ndocs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn),\nalready landed with the closely-related height-work safety pattern,\ncloned and read in full this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7133` as an OSS\ndocumentation/coordination actor for building structure cleaners,\nfollowing the same governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Building Cleaning\nCoordination Advisor ⊣ BldgCleanCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger. All source is portable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests\nare `clojure.test` `.clj`, matching the reference repo's own layout.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a fall-hazard/weather-condition/\n  equipment-condition/chemical-exposure concern, ALWAYS escalates,\n  NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- cleaning-materials/equipment\n  procurement proposal, escalates above a registered cost threshold\n\nNo op in this allowlist finalizes a cleaning-execution decision\n(including a height-work go/no-go call) or overrides a site-safety\nofficer's judgment -- these decision classes are structurally absent\nfrom the allowlist, not merely gated behind escalation.\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (`bldgclean.governor`, permanent, never\noverridable by human approval)\n\n1. **no-site** -- the job site named by the request must be\n   independently verified/registered before any action.\n2. **no-actuation** -- proposal `:effect` must be `:propose` (the\n   governor never dispatches hardware and never performs\n   building-cleaning work).\n3. **unknown-op** -- `:op` must be one of the four allowlisted\n   coordination ops; the closed op-allowlist is enforced\n   unconditionally.\n4. **site-mismatch** -- if the proposal names a site, it must be the\n   SAME site verified for this request (defense-in-depth against a\n   proposal quietly targeting an unverified site).\n5. **unknown-worker / worker-wrong-site** -- if the proposal\n   references a worker, that worker must be a REGISTERED crew member\n   belonging to this site.\n6. **scope-exclusion-violation** -- a proposal that attempts, in any\n   free-text field, to finalize a cleaning-execution decision\n   (including a height-work go/no-go call) or to override a\n   site-safety officer's judgment is a HARD, PERMANENT block,\n   evaluated unconditionally on content, independent of `:op`.\n\n### Escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (`bldgclean.governor/always-escalate-ops`). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a fall-hazard/\n  weather-condition/equipment-condition/chemical-exposure observation\n  -- it never resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-order-cost-threshold` (10000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-or-below-cost-threshold`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence.\n- advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` (0.6) also escalates,\n  for any op.\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare nouns (e.g.\n\"height\", \"cleaning\", \"chemical\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this risk is especially\nsharp here because this actor's ENTIRE domain is exterior building\ncleaning at height with chemical cleaning agents, so bare nouns like\n\"height\"/\"cleaning\"/\"chemical\" are ordinary, unavoidable vocabulary.\n`bldgclean.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTION PHRASES (e.g. \"proceed with the\nheight-work cleaning task\", \"finalize the height-work go/no-go\ndecision\", \"override the site safety officer's judgment\", \"bypass the\nchemical-exposure safety review\"), never bare nouns, and\n`bldgclean.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor (including a\n`:flag-safety-concern` request whose description names a fall hazard\n\"near the building edge at height\" and a second naming a \"strong\ncleaning-solution odor\"), never trips the scope-exclusion guard. A\ncompanion test, `scope-exclusion-not-triggered-by-bare-domain-nouns`,\nasserts directly against `governor/scope-exclusion-violation?` that a\nrationale/description containing only bare domain nouns (\"building\nfacade cleaning at height\" / \"fall-protection equipment and chemical\ncleaning-solution handling\") does not trip the guard, while four\ntrue-positive tests\n(`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-finalize-cleaning-execution`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-height-work-go-no-go`,\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-override-safety-officer` and\n`hard-and-permanent-on-scope-exclusion-bypass-chemical-safety-review`)\nconfirm the actual forbidden action phrases DO trip it, and\n`holds-a-scope-excluded-proposal-with-no-interrupt-path` confirms the\nfull actor graph resolves such an attempt straight to `:hold` (a\nfinish point, never `:request-approval`) with no record committed.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7133\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7133` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7133`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 25 tests, 63 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a fresh clone of the pushed repository (no mojibake in the\n  embedded Japanese governor-rule detail strings).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-7121`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-height-work-go-no-go` that is\n  merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops`: rejected outright per the\n  task's explicit height-work/chemical-cleaning-safety guidance and\n  the `ADR-2607152500`/`ADR-2799007121` precedent -- an always-escalate\n  op still means the *capability* to finalize a height-work go/no-go\n  or cleaning-execution decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision that can directly endanger\n  a worker's life or health at height or via chemical exposure, the\n  capability itself must not exist in the allowlist at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"height\" \"cleaning\"\n  \"chemical\"]`): rejected per the fleet-known self-trip bug class --\n  this actor's entire domain is exterior building cleaning at height\n  with chemical cleaning agents, so bare nouns would self-trip on\n  essentially every legitimate proposal (materials orders naming\n  \"cleaning solution\", safety flags naming a hazard \"at height\" or a\n  \"cleaning-solution odor\", etc.).\n- Checking site/worker provenance only from the proposal (never the\n  request): rejected -- the site-mismatch check requires the site\n  identity to be anchored at the request level and independently\n  cross-checked against anything the proposal claims, so a proposal\n  that quietly names a different, unverified site is caught even if\n  the proposal otherwise looks well-formed.\n- Modeling the worker-registration check as unconditionally required\n  on every op: rejected as too rigid -- `:coordinate-supply-order`\n  legitimately has no worker to reference (it is a materials-\n  procurement proposal against the site, not a person); the check\n  applies only when a proposal actually references a `:worker-id`.\n- Treating the chemical-exposure dimension as a separate op/allowlist\n  entry (e.g. `:flag-chemical-exposure`) distinct from\n  `:flag-safety-concern`: rejected as unnecessary complexity -- both\n  fall-hazard and chemical-exposure concerns are surfaced via the same\n  single always-escalate `:flag-safety-concern` op (disambiguated by\n  the free-text `:concern-type`), and both are covered by the same\n  unconditional human-sign-off gate; splitting the op would not change\n  the escalation semantics, only add allowlist surface area.\n")))
